### What I don't have

The tone of this article may lead you to think that I feel that this model is above reroach, but that is far from the truth. The reality is that general relativity (GR) produces accuracies that this model fails to reproduce independently, but this model _does_ reproduce the _geometry_ of GR in the coordinate system of the observer in relative motion as measured by the observer in relative rest, therefore repdroducing an equivalent geometry in precisely the coordinate system where relativistic effects would be expected.

